From c4c7b4989b3cb1df7720dae308ab31bdc3bda718 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:47:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 54/55] kubelet/volumemanager: retry the cleanup of volumes
 that failed reconstruction

cleanOrphanVolumes was one-shot: it scheduled one UnmountVolume per
volume that could not be reconstructed after a kubelet restart, then
forgot the volume. The cleanup runs right after the kubelet starts,
possibly before the containers of a pod deleted while the kubelet was
down are killed. On FreeBSD a container's nullfs mount of a subPath
keeps the kubelet's mount below it busy (Linux mount namespaces hold
copies), so the unmount failed with EBUSY and the volume stayed mounted
until the next kubelet restart (e2e: "should unmount if pod is force
deleted while kubelet is down").

Keep such a volume while its directory is still on disk and try again
every 10s for 5 minutes; cleanupMounts no longer logs the operation
executor's expected "pending"/backoff errors.
